# Conversation Feature: Proposed Optimizations and Future Enhancements

_This rule is for manual attachment only. It lists optimizations and features not included in the initial proof of concept for conversational scenarios, but which are desirable for future development._

## Optimizations and Features to Consider
- Allow user to specify the number of lines/turns in a conversation (not just 2–4 by default)
- Let user choose or randomize speaker voices (beyond the default two)
- Support more than two speakers in a conversation
- Allow user to set the pause duration between lines in merged audio
- Batch phrase generation and audio synthesis to avoid duplicate phrases and reduce API calls
- Deduplicate phrases across conversations to save storage and avoid redundant audio generation
- Add user accounts and make conversations user-specific
- Enable editing or deleting conversations and lines after creation
- Add tagging or categorization for conversations (e.g., travel, shopping, emergencies)
- Support exporting conversations as downloadable audio or text
- Add progress tracking or spaced repetition for conversation practice
- Improve error handling and user feedback for TTS/translation failures
- Add analytics for most-used phrases or scenarios
- Support additional languages or dialects

_This list should be reviewed and updated as the feature evolves._
